        "structuredContent": {
          "modules": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "<p>In this tour, our curators will guide you around our new exhibition “<a href=\"https://www.thelondonarchives.org/visit-us/exhibitions/londoners-on-trial\" title=\"https://www.thelondonarchives.org/visit-us/exhibitions/londoners-on-trial\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Londoners on Trial: Crime, Courts and the Public 1244-1924</a>”, exploring the history of law and order in London, uncovering the stories of London’s criminals and victims and demonstrating how historical records relating to crime can illuminate the lives and streets of London past.</p><p>The curator-led tour lasts approximately 45 minutes and there will be an opportunity to ask questions. After the tour you’ll have plenty of time to explore the exhibition by yourself.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><strong>Please note:</strong></strong> we run regular public Curator tours on selected Tuesdays and Saturdays each month. Spaces are limited. We are currently booking for tours taking place to December 2026 - and Eventbrite will only show tour dates that still have tickets available.</p><ul><li>Our new exhibition <a href=\"https://www.thelondonarchives.org/visit-us/exhibitions/londoners-on-trial\" title=\"https://www.thelondonarchives.org/visit-us/exhibitions/londoners-on-trial\" target=\"_blank\" data-msys-clicktrack=\"0\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">\"Londoners on Trial: Crime, Courts and the Public 1244-1924\"</a> runs from 9 March 2026 until 25 February 2027. It is free to visit without a curator-led tour.</li></ul><ul><li>Please contact ask@tla.libanswers.com if you'd like to enquire about a curator-led tour for a private group, or if you intend to visit the exhibition with a group of 7 or more without a tour.</li><li>These curator-led exhibition tours<strong><strong> take place within the Exhibition Space </strong></strong>where the curator can discuss individual items on display, and visitors will be expected to stand and move around the space. Chairs can be made available for those who need them(see FAQs). Visitors using wheelchairs or other mobility equipment are welcome.</li><li>The Exhibition Space will be open to other members of the public (and staff) during these tours, although we will try to keep any disruption to a minimum.</li></ul>",
              "alignment": "left",
              "url": null,
              "alt": null,
              "caption": null,
              "imageId": null,
              "originalUrl": null,
              "width": null,
              "height": null,
              "embedUrl": null
            }
          ],
          "widgets": {
            "faqs": [
              {
                "question": "Where does the curator-led exhibition tour take place? ",
                "answer": "All curator-led exhibition tours take place in the Exhibition, where the curator will discuss individual items on display throughout the space. Please note that the Exhibition will be open to other members of the public (and staff) although we will try to keep disruption to a minimum."
              },
              {
                "question": "Do I need to move or stand during the curator-led exhibition tour?",
                "answer": "As the curator-led exhibition tour takes place in the Exhibition, visitors should expect to stand and move around the space. Chairs can be made available for those who need them, please ask the curator when you arrive or email ask@tla.libanswers.com in advance. Visitors using wheelchairs are welcome"
              },
              {
                "question": "Any other questions about accessibility?",
                "answer": "The exhibition space is accessible by stairs or lift. An accessible toilet is on the same floor. Further details on www.thelondonarchives.org/visit-us/accessibility and please contact us at ask@tla.libanswers.com if you have any specific accessibility requirements. "
              },
              {
                "question": "The cost of the ticket is preventing me from attending - how can I join?",
                "answer": "If the price of the ticket is preventing you from attending then please contact us at TLADigital@cityoflondon.gov.uk"
              },
              {
                "question": "Do you offer curator-led tours for groups?",
                "answer": "We may be able to offer curator-led tours of the exhibition for groups for a small charge, depending on staff availability - please enquire by email ask@tla.libanswers.com ."
              },
              {
                "question": "Do I need to make a booking for a group visit if we don't need a tour?",
                "answer": "Yes, groups of over 6 people need to make a group booking to visit the exhibition itself. There is no charge to visit without a tour, however pre-booking helps us manage capacity. Please contact ask@tla.libanswers.com with the proposed date, time, and group size."
              }
            ],
